  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "php_var_dump",
    "file": "php-src/ext/standard/var.c",
    "description": "`php_var_dump()` iterates an object\u2019s debug properties hash table (`myht`) and recursively dumps each property value. During this iteration, userland `__destruct()` re-enters `var_dump($this)` and then executes `unset($this->children)`, which destroys array elements and can free referenced child objects that are still being traversed by the outer `php_var_dump` call. The outer traversal then dereferences a stale/freed zval/object pointer (seen at `var.c:149` via `Z_OBJCE_P(struc)`), causing a heap-use-after-free.",
    "conditions": "PoV creates cyclic object references via dynamic property assignment (`$node->\\xff = $this`) and stores children in `$this->children[]`. On shutdown, destructors run; inside `Node::__destruct`, calling `var_dump($this)` causes recursive property traversal, and `unset($this->children)` mutates/frees the same object graph during traversal. This re-entrancy + mutation of properties being dumped leads to UAF in `php_var_dump` when it continues recursion on freed child objects."
  },
